e response, so if you hit it from a browser, it'll prompt to save as `profile_export_[timestamp].json`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:43] Charlie**: @Bob helps a lot with the CLI parity work I'm doing. I can basically pipe this straight into the local engine for debugging.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:46] Alice**: Great work everyone. Calling this done — export matches the REST contract.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:49] Bob**: :raised_hands:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 47 slack thread redact profil export verif channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 16 2026 08 16 14 35 diana final verif on the redact profil export is look solid i check the export payload against the rest api contract and the field line up with what bob ship for the exist endpoint 2026 08 16 16 18 alic awesom diana did you test it with the larg profil we generat for the stress test ani latenc issu 2026 08 16 16 26 diana latenc is neglig sinc it s just a json dump the largest one about 4mb came back in under 150ms 2026 08 16 17 42 bob i also ad a content disposit header to the respons so if you hit it from a browser it ll prompt to save a profil _ export _ timestamp json 2026 08 16 17 43 charli bob help a lot with the cli pariti work i m do i can basic pipe this straight into the local engin for debug 2026 08 16 17 46 alic great work everyon call this done export match the rest contract 2026 08 16 17 49 bob rais _ hand\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edbde0848a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"id\": \"5ed77310c4e63c72\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3298763735100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6217654, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edbde0848a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1141, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:17\", \"token_count\": 338, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"7d969f7c78a9200e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_