45 (GUI Wrapper for CLI), for desktop users who don't want a command-line entry point.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-29\\n\\n# Document: Electron-Shell-Scaffold-Review\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2029\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-14)\\n\\n## Electron Scaffold\\n\\nEvan put together a minimal Electron shell that spawns the existing CLI engine as a child process and streams its stdout back into a simple window, rather than reimplementing any redaction logic in the GUI layer. Wrapping the CLI as a subprocess keeps the wrapper thin and means the GUI inherits every CLI fix and feature without duplicated logic.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-29\\n\\n# Document: Electron-Shell-Scaffold-Review\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2029\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-14)\\n\\n## Open item at this stage\\n\\nAt the time this scaffold was put together, the wrapper had not yet been packaged or run through a package test; that came afterward and is not part of this scaffold note.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 29 document electron shell scaffold review owner evan document key doc 2029 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 14 decis note note on the initi electron shell scaffold 2026 08 14 for ciph 45 gui wrapper for cli for desktop user who don t want a command line entri point sourc id src gdoc 29 document electron shell scaffold review owner evan document key doc 2029 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 14 electron scaffold evan put togeth a minim electron shell that spawn the exist cli engin a a child process and stream it stdout back into a simpl window rather than reimplement ani redact logic in the gui layer wrap the cli a a subprocess keep the wrapper thin and mean the gui inherit everi cli fix and featur without duplic logic sourc id src gdoc 29 document electron shell scaffold review owner evan document key doc 2029 last updat 2026 0831 retrospe