erything the OCR branch can reach on its own.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 10:49] Diana**: I'll run it against the QA scenario that left orphaned files last week and see if it actually clears them.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 09:09] Diana**: Confirmed — ran it through both the failure case and a normal completion, and the temp files are gone after each. No leftovers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 09:30] Charlie**: Good. Secure deletion confirmed — I'll close this out.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 29 slack thread ocr temp cleanup hook channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 09 last activ 2026 08 11 2026 08 09 09 21 charli cleanup hook are in cover both the failur path and the normal complet path use the site inventori from the trace so noth s left out 2026 08 09 09 36 bob what happen if the process get kill outright instead of fail clean 2026 08 09 09 39 charli can t hook a hard kill direct but between the failur hook and the complet hook we cover everyth the ocr branch can reach on it own 2026 08 09 10 49 diana i ll run it against the qa scenario that left orphan file last week and see if it actual clear them 2026 08 11 09 09 diana confirm ran it through both the failur case and a normal complet and the temp file are gone after each no leftov 2026 08 11 09 30 charli good secur delet confirm i ll close this out\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edbfe9608a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"id\": \"c2cece11a183981b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33014143851005684, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.62264895, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edbfe9608a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1012, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:16\", \"token_count\": 297, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-08\\n\\n# Slack Thread: API Authentication Deferral\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:07] Bob**: Looking into REST API auth for v1.0. Do we need a full auth story now, or is trusted local network enough for the first release?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:22] Diana**: Given the PII involved, something robust would be nice. But if this is strictly local-network-only, we might not need it for v1.0.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 14:00] Bob**: Doing a short study either way — what we'd need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-29 14:23] Diana**: If we defer, we should at least write down the v1.1 requirements so we don't lose them.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:01] Alice**: Team, we're falling behind on core engine work. I'm deferring the auth module to v1.1. For v1.0, the API assumes a trusted local network.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:19] Diana**: Manageable if we stay local-network-only. I'll note the deferral.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:21] Bob**: Fine. I'll keep the seams clean so adding auth later isn't a rewrite.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:04] Bob**: Still deferred — capturing v1.1 auth requirements while we remember them: REST auth with rotation support, since v1.0 is local-network-only.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:06] Diana**: Agreed. Folding that into the deferred-work notes so it survives until v1.1 planning.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:11] Alice**: Rechecked release scope for v1.0 — auth stays deferred to post-v1.0.0. Trusted-network assumption still holds.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 08 slack thread api authent deferr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 06 28 13 07 bob look into rest api auth for v1 0 do we need a full auth stori now or is trust local network enough for the first releas 2026 06 28 13 22 diana given the pii involv someth robust would be nice but if this is strict local network onli we might not need it for v1 0 2026 06 28 14 00 bob do a short studi either way what we d need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer 2026 06 29 14 23 diana if we defer we should at least write down the v1 1 requir so we don t lose them 2026 06 30 09 01 alic team we re fall behind on core engin work i m defer the auth modul to v1 1 for v1 0 the api assum a trust local network 2026 06 30 09 19 diana manag if we stay local network onli i ll note the deferr 2026 06 30 09 21 bob fine i ll keep the seam clean so ad auth later isn t a rewrit 2026 08 0511 04 bob still defer captur v1 1 auth requir while we rememb them rest auth with rotat support sinc v1 0 is local network onli 2026 08 0511 06 diana agre fold that into the defer work note so it surviv until v1 1 plan 2026 08 20 10 11 alic recheck releas scope for v1 0 auth stay defer to post v1 0 0 trust network assumpt still hold\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ede967228a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"id\": \"6268e33c2ef3a618\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3285276785100568, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.61726975, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ede967228a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1525, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:39\", \"token_count\": 479, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-45\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Redaction Profile Schema\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:29] Bob**: Designing an exportable schema for the redaction profile — dictionary versions, regex patterns, thresholds, everything that went into a given batch, so it can be reviewed later.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:32] Alice**: This is the piece that makes redaction decisions reproducible for compliance, right? If someone asks why a name got redacted, we need to be able to show the exact rule.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:38] Bob**: Exactly the goal — a machine-readable export of everything that fired.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 12:09] Charlie**: Are you including the engine version in it? Regex behavior can shift slightly between versions.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 12:12] Bob**: Good call, adding that to the schema.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 12:13] Diana**: What about custom dictionaries someone's added locally? Do those need to be part of the export too?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 12:54] Bob**: They have to be, otherwise the profile's incomplete. Still working out the shape of the schema before I touch the export endpoint itself.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 45 slack thread redact profil schema channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 11 29 bob design an export schema for the redact profil dictionari version regex pattern threshold everyth that went into a given batch so it can be review later 2026 08 12 11 32 alic this is the piec that make redact decis reproduc for complianc right if someon ask whi a name got redact we need to be abl to show the exact rule 2026 08 12 11 38 bob exact the goal a machin readabl export of everyth that fire 2026 08 12 12 09 charli are you includ the engin version in it regex behavior can shift slight between version 2026 08 12 12 12 bob good call ad that to the schema 2026 08 12 12 13 diana what about custom dictionari someon s ad local do those need to be part of the export too 2026 08 12 12 54 bob they have to be otherwis the profil s incomplet still work out the shape of the schema befor i touch the export endpoint itself\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edee88ec8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-redaction-profile-schema.md\", \"id\": \"c2c1ad218115bdfe\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32548218351005687, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6071181, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-redaction-profile-schema.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edee88ec8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-redaction-profile-schema.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-redaction-profile-schema.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1125, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:34\", \"token_count\": 322, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-50\\n\\n# Slack Thread: CSV Dictionary Loader\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:21] Bob**: Working on the CSV loader for custom dictionary support. I'm thinking we support a simple two-column format: `term,tag`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:29] Charlie**: Can we support regex in the dictionary too, or is it strictly string matching?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:40] Bob**: For the first pass, I'm just doing exact string matches and case-insensitive substrings. Regex in the dictionary might blow up the processing time if the list gets huge.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:41] Alice**: @Bob we need to make sure this works with the existing HIPAA identifiers. If a user adds a custom name to the dictionary, it should be treated with the same priority.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:00] Bob**: Definitely. The `DictionaryMatcher` will run alongside the regex engine.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:30] Diana**: @Bob what happens if there's a comma in the term? Standard CSV escaping?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:32] Bob**: Yeah, I'm using the Python `csv` module with `QUOTE_MINIMAL`. I'll add a test case for quoted terms.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 50 slack thread csv dictionari loader channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 11 21 bob work on the csv loader for custom dictionari support i m think we support a simpl two column format term tag 2026 08 12 11 29 charli can we support regex in the dictionari too or is it strict string match 2026 08 12 11 40 bob for the first pas i m just do exact string match and case insensit substr regex in the dictionari might blow up the process time if the list get huge 2026 08 12 11 41 alic bob we need to make sure this work with the exist hipaa identifi if a user add a custom name to the dictionari it should be treat with the same prioriti 2026 08 12 13 00 bob definit the dictionarymatch will run alongsid the regex engin 2026 08 12 13 30 diana bob what happen if there s a comma in the term standard csv escap 2026 08 12 13 32 bob yeah i m use the python csv modul with quot _ minim i ll add a test case for quot term\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edc9244e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"id\": \"d9aa72bd1d956a20\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3246999335100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6045106, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edc9244e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1112, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:07\", \"token_count\": 335, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-15\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Local Runtime Static Compile\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 08:58] Evan**: Static-link study pointed at a full static compile, so I went ahead and built the local runtime binary that way.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:30] Evan**: It builds and runs locally. Next step is confirming it's actually clean of external shared-lib dependencies before we call this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:31] Alice**: Nice progress. Diana, can you run the verification pass?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:29] Diana**: Verified — the static binary runs without pulling in any external shared libraries. That satisfies the air-gap packaging requirement for the static-link work.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:32] Evan**: Calling this done on my end too.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 15 slack thread local runtim static compil channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 04 last activ 2026 08 05 2026 08 04 08 58 evan static link studi point at a full static compil so i went ahead and built the local runtim binari that way 2026 08 04 10 30 evan it build and run local next step is confirm it s actual clean of extern share lib depend befor we call this done 2026 08 04 10 31 alic nice progress diana can you run the verif pas 2026 08 0511 29 diana verifi the static binari run without pull in ani extern share librari that satisfi the air gap packag requir for the static link work 2026 08 0511 32 evan call this done on my end too\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee2549cc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-local-runtime-static-compile.md\", \"id\": \"bd735e197ebf2df1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3236025185100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.60085255, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-local-runtime-static-compile.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee2549cc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-local-runtime-static-compile.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-local-runtime-static-compile.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 813, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:41\", \"token_count\": 243, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-28\\n\\n# Custom Dictionary: CSV Loader Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2028\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-29\\n\\n*Retrospective note: summarizes the 2026-08-12 CSV dictionary loader for T034; written up today.*\\n\\nOperators asked for org-specific redaction terms without forking the built-in pattern set. The chosen path is a user-supplied CSV dictionary that the engine can load alongside existing detection rules.\\n\\n## Loader in place\\n\\nOn 2026-08-12 Bob implemented the CSV dictionary loader so those site-specific terms can be ingested into the pipeline. That closes the “how do we get custom terms into the process” question for the loader layer.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-28\\n\\n# Custom Dictionary: CSV Loader Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2028\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-29\\n\\n*Retrospective note: summarizes the 2026-08-12 CSV dictionary loader for T034; written up today.*\\n\\nOperators asked for org-specific redaction terms without forking the built-in pattern set. The chosen path is a user-supplied CSV dictionary that the engine can load alongside existing detection rules.\\n\\n## What this does not cover\\n\\nMatcher wiring and a formal rule-test pass are separate follow-ons. This note does not claim that custom terms already fire correctly end-to-end—only that the loader exists and T034 was Active at the time of that implementation.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 28 custom dictionari csv loader note owner bob document key doc 2028 last updat 2026 08 29 retrospect note summar the 2026 08 12 csv dictionari loader for t034 written up today oper ask for org specif redact term without fork the built in pattern set the chosen path is a user suppli csv dictionari that the engin can load alongsid exist detect rule loader in place on 2026 08 12 bob implement the csv dictionari loader so those site specif term can be ingest into the pipelin that close the how do we get custom term into the process question for the loader layer sourc id src gdoc 28 custom dictionari csv loader note owner bob document key doc 2028 last updat 2026 08 29 retrospect note summar the 2026 08 12 csv dictionari loader for t034 written up today oper ask for org specif redact term without fork the built in pattern set the chosen path is a user suppli csv dictionari that the engin can load alongsid exist detect rule what this doe not cover matcher wire and a formal rule test pas are separ follow on this note doe not claim that custom term alreadi fire correct end to end onli that the loader exist and t034 wa activ at the time of that implement\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eec0de3c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-29-Custom-Dictionary-Support-Review.md\", \"id\": \"97ea07b4be76e080\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3227740535100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.598091, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-29-Custom-Dictionary-Support-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eec0de3c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-29-Custom-Dictionary-Support-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-29-Custom-Dictionary-Support-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 937, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:27\", \"token_count\": 339, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 1