rces/2026-08-08-PII-Pattern-HIPAA-Verification-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eecb68848a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-08-PII-Pattern-HIPAA-Verification-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-08-PII-Pattern-HIPAA-Verification-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 963, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:18\", \"token_count\": 468, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## What was prototyped\\n\\nA handshake in which each node presents a signed challenge/response before either side accepts replication traffic from the other. No central node is required to bootstrap trust between two peers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Result as of 2026-08-06\\n\\nThe handshake completed reliably across every run on a single LAN segment with nominal round-trip latency. No cross-node encryption mismatches or handshake rejections were seen at that stage.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Open question\\n\\nThe prototype has only been exercised on one LAN segment. Whether the handshake holds up across a simulated multi-site link with realistic latency and jitter has not been tested and is the planned next step before this can support multi-site rollout.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy what wa prototyp a handshak in which each node present a sign challeng respons befor either side accept replic traffic from the other no central node is requir to bootstrap trust between two peer sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy result a of 2026 08 06 the handshak complet reliabl across everi run on a singl lan segment with nomin round trip latenc no cross node encrypt mismatch or handshak reject were seen at that stage sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy open question the prototyp ha onli been exercis on one lan segment whether the handshak hold up across a simul multi site link with realist latenc and jitter ha not been test and is the plan next step befor this can support multi site rollout\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eec9d0788a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"id\": \"93691740b3cc2cb4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3909785068083519, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2833422382976456, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6421298, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eec9d0788a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1055, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:18\", \"token_count\": 453, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-11\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Manual Review Threshold Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:08] Diana**: Starting on the manual review threshold work. We need a safety valve for when the engine isn't confident about a redaction. I'm proposing a 90% confidence threshold — anything below that gets flagged for manual review.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:55] Charlie**: How do we define \\\"confidence\\\"? Just the regex match score, or are we factoring in OCR quality too?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 10:09] Diana**: Both. If the OCR engine gives a low confidence score for a block of text, we should flag it regardless of the regex match.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:49] Diana**: Picking this back up — implementing the quarantine folder now. Docs that fall below the 90% threshold land there and won't be exported until a human confirms the redaction.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:35] Diana**: Quarantine folder alone doesn't give reviewers enough context. Designing the metadata that goes with each quarantined file: confidence score, page number, and the reason it was flagged.\\n\\n**[2026-09-05 14:34] Charlie**: Added visual indicators in the UI for quarantined pages, tied to that metadata, so reviewers can see at a glance why a page was held.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:55] Diana**: Ran an end-to-end pass: detection -> quarantine -> metadata -> UI markers -> manual approval. The pipeline holds together, but the 90% threshold tuning itself is still in progress — I want another round of testing before I'd call it locked.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:58] Charlie**: Makes sense. Let me know when you want another look at the UI side once the threshold settles.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 11 slack thread manual review threshold design channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 06 28 09 08 diana start on the manual review threshold work we need a safeti valv for when the engin isn t confid about a redact i m propos a 90 confid threshold anyth below that get flag for manual review 2026 06 28 09 55 charli how do we defin confid just the regex match score or are we factor in ocr qualiti too 2026 06 28 10 09 diana both if the ocr engin give a low confid score for a block of text we should flag it regardless of the regex match 2026 08 06 10 49 diana pick this back up implement the quarantin folder now doc that fall below the 90 threshold land there and won t be export until a human confirm the redact 2026 08 20 13 35 diana quarantin folder alon doesn t give review enough context design the metadata that go with each quarantin file confid score page number and the reason it wa flag 2026 09 05 14 34 charli ad visual indic in the ui for quarantin page tie to that metadata so review can see at a glanc whi a page wa held 2026 09 18 15 55 diana ran an end to end pas detect quarantin metadata ui marker manual approv the pipelin hold togeth but the 90 threshold tune itself is still in progress i want anoth round of test befor i d call it lock 2026 09 18 15 58 charli make sens let me know when you want anoth look at the ui side onc the threshold settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0973008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"id\": \"b1a90ff76c3fb32a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3281189825100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.61590743, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0973008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1695, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:09\", \"token_count\": 460, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-02\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Regex Library Selection and Pattern Fix\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-06\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 10:42] Charlie**: Looking at the regex detection work. Standard library `re` in Python is too slow for the volume we're expecting. I'm proposing we use `hyperscan` or `google/re2`.\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 11:30] Diana**: I'd lean toward `re2` for the safety guarantees. We can't afford a ReDoS vulnerability in a redaction engine.\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 11:35] Charlie**: Agreed. `re2` it is.\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 11:36] Alice**: Ack.\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 14:15] Diana**: @Charlie I just ran the initial SSN pattern against the test set. It's failing on the 1970s format with dashes. Looks like the lookahead is too strict.\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 14:32] Charlie**: Dang, you're right. Let me check the HIPAA spec again. \\n\\n**[2026-06-06 14:33] Charlie**: Updated the pattern to `\\\\b\\\\d{3}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{4}\\\\b`. The previous one was missing the word boundary check, which was causing false positives on longer digit strings too.\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 14:34] Diana**: Much better. Still seeing a slight lag on the 50MB file.\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 14:36] Charlie**: Just pushed the pattern fix. Optimized the DFA compilation for the compiled regexes. Should see a noticeable speedup on large batches.\\n\\n**[2026-06-06 14:37] Diana**: Verified. Done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 02 slack thread regex librari select and pattern fix channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 06 2026 06 06 10 42 charli look at the regex detect work standard librari re in python is too slow for the volum we re expect i m propos we use hyperscan or googl re2 2026 06 06 11 30 diana i d lean toward re2 for the safeti guarante we can t afford a redo vulner in a redact engin 2026 06 06 11 35 charli agre re2 it is 2026 06 06 11 36 alic ack 2026 06 06 14 15 diana charli i just ran the initi ssn pattern against the test set it s fail on the 1970s format with dash look like the lookahead is too strict 2026 06 06 14 32 charli dang you re right let me check the hipaa spec again 2026 06 06 14 33 charli updat the pattern to b d3 d2 d4 b the previous one wa miss the word boundari check which wa caus fals posit on longer digit string too 2026 06 06 14 34 diana much better still see a slight lag on the 50mb file 2026 06 06 14 36 charli just push the pattern fix optim the dfa compil for the compil regex should see a notic speedup on larg batch 2026 06 06 14 37 diana verifi done\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee23beae8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-06-regex-dependency.md\", \"id\": \"6a0b6d88904458a9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32730999351005685, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6132108, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-06-regex-dependency.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee23beae8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-06-regex-dependency.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-06-regex-dependency.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1335, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:44\", \"token_count\": 433, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-48\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Memory Leak Hotspots\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-17\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:16] Bob**: Running into some weirdness with memory. The long-running container is hitting the memory limit after about 4 hours of processing. Looks like a slow leak.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:34] Charlie**: Is it in the engine or the API layer? If we're not clearing the regex caches, that could be it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:37] Bob**: I'm seeing the RSS climb even when the API is idle after a batch. I suspect something in the `DocumentProcessor` isn't closing file handles or clearing buffers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:38] Charlie**: Ugh.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:50] Diana**: I can confirm this on the staging node. I've been watching the Grafana dashboard and it's a steady 45-degree angle upward. No dips.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:15] Evan**: I've bumped the limit to 2GB temporarily so we don't keep crashing, but we need a real fix. @Bob are you using `tracemalloc` yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:16] Bob**: Just starting a run with it now. I'll dump the snapshots and see where the allocations are sticking.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:17] Alice**: @Bob if this is a deep issue in the engine core, we might need to pull Charlie in full-time on this.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:18] Charlie**: Already looking at the `pdfminer` wrappers. We've had issues with its object recycling before.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 48 slack thread memori leak hotspot channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 17 2026 08 17 10 16 bob run into some weird with memori the long run contain is hit the memori limit after about 4 hour of process look like a slow leak 2026 08 17 10 34 charli is it in the engin or the api layer if we re not clear the regex cach that could be it 2026 08 17 10 37 bob i m see the rss climb even when the api is idl after a batch i suspect someth in the documentprocessor isn t close file handl or clear buffer 2026 08 17 10 38 charli ugh 2026 08 17 10 50 diana i can confirm this on the stage node i ve been watch the grafana dashboard and it s a steadi 45 degre angl upward no dip 2026 08 17 11 15 evan i ve bump the limit to 2gb temporarili so we don t keep crash but we need a real fix bob are you use tracemalloc yet 2026 08 17 11 16 bob just start a run with it now i ll dump the snapshot and see where the alloc are stick 2026 08 17 11 17 alic bob if this is a deep issu in the engin core we might need to pull charli in full time on this 2026 08 17 11 18 charli alreadi look at the pdfminer wrapper we ve had issu with it object recycl befor\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edeb07bc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-memory-leak-hotspots.md\", \"id\": \"f8eeaf3fd344f2f9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32348596851005684, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.60046405, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-memory-leak-hotspots.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edeb07bc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-memory-leak-hotspots.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-memory-leak-hotspots.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1370, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:36\", \"token_count\": 421, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-34\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Benchmark Scripts\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 10:08] Evan**: Writing the bare-metal benchmark scripts now — need something repeatable we can rerun on a real local node, not one-off numbers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 10:11] Alice**: These are for the release performance claims, right? Make sure they're something we can rerun later and get the same shape of result.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 10:44] Evan**: That's the goal — same script, same inputs, comparable output every time.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 10:46] Charlie**: Yep.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 11:59] Charlie**: Are you testing across file types, or just one?\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 12:16] Evan**: Multiple — want to see if the timing holds up consistently, not just on the easy case.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 12:19] Alice**: Sounds good.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 34 slack thread benchmark script channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 07 2026 08 07 10 08 evan write the bare metal benchmark script now need someth repeat we can rerun on a real local node not one off number 2026 08 07 10 11 alic these are for the releas perform claim right make sure they re someth we can rerun later and get the same shape of result 2026 08 07 10 44 evan that s the goal same script same input compar output everi time 2026 08 07 10 46 charli yep 2026 08 07 11 59 charli are you test across file type or just one 2026 08 07 12 16 evan multipl want to see if the time hold up consist not just on the easi case 2026 08 07 12 19 alic sound good\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee2bd3328a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-07-benchmark-scripts.md\", \"id\": \"f81c1a3ab9c6282a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3231027035100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.5991865, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-07-benchmark-scripts.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee2bd3328a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-07-benchmark-scripts.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-07-benchmark-scripts.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 827, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:36\", \"token_count\": 267, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-55\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Electron Package Test\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 14:17] Diana**: Just finished the final packaging tests for the GUI. It's running smooth on both the dev machine and the clean test VM.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 15:13] Alice**: Does it include the latest build of the engine with the memory leak fix?\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 15:15] Evan**: Yep, I pulled in the latest binary from the CI pipeline before building the installer.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 16:28] Bob**: I tested the config import/export through the GUI too. It's correctly loading the YAML profiles from the configuration directory.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 16:31] Alice**: Calling the package test done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 16:34] Bob**: Nice.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 16:50] Evan**: :raised_hands:\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 16:53] Charlie**: Great work Evan. The UI looks really polished.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 55 slack thread electron packag test channel releas date 2026 08 18 2026 08 18 14 17 diana just finish the final packag test for the gui it s run smooth on both the dev machin and the clean test vm 2026 08 18 15 13 alic doe it includ the latest build of the engin with the memori leak fix 2026 08 18 1515 evan yep i pull in the latest binari from the ci pipelin befor build the instal 2026 08 18 16 28 bob i test the config import export through the gui too it s correct load the yaml profil from the configur directori 2026 08 18 16 31 alic call the packag test done 2026 08 18 16 34 bob nice 2026 08 18 16 50 evan rais _ hand 2026 08 18 16 53 charli great work evan the ui look realli polish\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee28afe08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-electron-package-test.md\", \"id\": \"e70fec23741733fb\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32185695351005683, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.595034, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-electron-package-test.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee28afe08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-electron-package-test.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-electron-package-test.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 869, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:39\", \"token_count\": 281, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-65\\n\\n# Slack Thread: A11y Keyboard Navigation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 10:07] Diana**: Starting the a11y audit. First pass on keyboard navigation in the Electron app isn't great. You can't tab into the redaction preview pane at all.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 10:08] Evan**: That's because it's a custom Canvas-based renderer. We'll need to implement an ARIA-compliant layer on top of it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 10:34] Alice**: @Evan, how much work is that? We're already pretty tight on the GUI schedule.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 10:37] Diana**: It's not just the preview. The sidebar buttons don't have hover states or clear focus indicators either.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 10:38] Bob**: I can help with the CSS for the focus rings, but Evan needs to handle the Canvas accessibility.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 10:43] Alice**: Let's prioritize the most critical paths. If we can get the main controls accessible, that's a win for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 65 slack thread a11y keyboard navig channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 21 2026 08 21 10 07 diana start the a11y audit first pas on keyboard navig in the electron app isn t great you can t tab into the redact preview pane at all 2026 08 21 10 08 evan that s becaus it s a custom canva base render we ll need to implement an aria compliant layer on top of it 2026 08 21 10 34 alic evan how much work is that we re alreadi pretti tight on the gui schedul 2026 08 21 10 37 diana it s not just the preview the sidebar button don t have hover state or clear focus indic either 2026 08 21 10 38 bob i can help with the cs for the focus ring but evan need to handl the canva access 2026 08 21 10 43 alic let s priorit the most critic path if we can get the main control access that s a win for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edfdf26e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-a11y-keyboard.md\", \"id\": \"0333976fef0a12f3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3204233135100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.5902552, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-a11y-keyboard.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edfdf26e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-a11y-keyboard.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-a11y-keyboard.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 950, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:21\", \"token_count\": 296, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-37\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Title**: Validate batch runs under a network-denied harness\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild a reproducible offline test harness that denies network access, then execute a full batch run under it to validate the strict air-gapped claim, depending on the completed AES-256 encryption pipeline. The offline batch run completed and was signed off, with a noted 45-second remote licence-check hang recorded; this sign-off is preliminary only and is not a compliance certification.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-37\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Title**: Validate batch runs under a network-denied harness\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Offline test harness reliably denies network access during a batch run.\\n\\n- Full batch executes successfully to completion under the harness with network blocked.\\n\\n- Sign-off explicitly notes it is preliminary and not a compliance certification, along with the observed licence-check hang.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-37\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Title**: Validate batch runs under a network-denied harness\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild a reproducible offline test harness that denies network access, then execute a full batch run under it to validate the strict air-gapped claim, depending on the completed AES-256 encryption pipeline. The offline batch run completed and was signed off, with a noted 45-second remote licence-check hang recorded; this sign-off is preliminary only and is not a compliance certification.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-37\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Title**: Validate batch runs under a network-denied harness\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-04**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 37 sourc id src cu c