urce ID**: SRC-SLACK-40\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License AGPL Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:14] Diana**: Reopening the license review. The PDF parser Evan swapped in to clear the earlier audit finding turns out to be AGPL-licensed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:01] Alice**: AGPL is a dealbreaker for how we distribute this. Are we sure about the licensing?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:03] Diana**: Sure — checked the license file directly. It's not something we can ship under our current distribution model.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:31] Charlie**: Is there a non-copyleft alternative that covers the same parsing we need?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:33] Alice**: Please look.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:08] Diana**: Looking now. Putting this back in progress until we land on a replacement that passes a clean scan.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 40 slack thread licens agpl reopen channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 14 diana reopen the licens review the pdf parser evan swap in to clear the earlier audit find turn out to be agpl licens 2026 08 12 1001 alic agpl is a dealbreak for how we distribut this are we sure about the licens 2026 08 12 1003 diana sure check the licens file direct it s not someth we can ship under our current distribut model 2026 08 12 10 31 charli is there a non copyleft altern that cover the same pars we need 2026 08 12 10 33 alic pleas look 2026 08 12 11 08 diana look now put this back in progress until we land on a replac that pass a clean scan\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee1f112e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"939b461988ef2eb1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32570514351005686, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6078613, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee1f112e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-license-agpl-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 813, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:49\", \"token_count\": 257, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-50\\n\\n# Slack Thread: CSV Dictionary Loader\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:21] Bob**: Working on the CSV loader for custom dictionary support. I'm thinking we support a simple two-column format: `term,tag`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:29] Charlie**: Can we support regex in the dictionary too, or is it strictly string matching?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:40] Bob**: For the first pass, I'm just doing exact string matches and case-insensitive substrings. Regex in the dictionary might blow up the processing time if the list gets huge.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:41] Alice**: @Bob we need to make sure this works with the existing HIPAA identifiers. If a user adds a custom name to the dictionary, it should be treated with the same priority.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:00] Bob**: Definitely. The `DictionaryMatcher` will run alongside the regex engine.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:30] Diana**: @Bob what happens if there's a comma in the term? Standard CSV escaping?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:32] Bob**: Yeah, I'm using the Python `csv` module with `QUOTE_MINIMAL`. I'll add a test case for quoted terms.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 50 slack thread csv dictionari loader channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 11 21 bob work on the csv loader for custom dictionari support i m think we support a simpl two column format term tag 2026 08 12 11 29 charli can we support regex in the dictionari too or is it strict string match 2026 08 12 11 40 bob for the first pas i m just do exact string match and case insensit substr regex in the dictionari might blow up the process time if the list get huge 2026 08 12 11 41 alic bob we need to make sure this work with the exist hipaa identifi if a user add a custom name to the dictionari it should be treat with the same prioriti 2026 08 12 13 00 bob definit the dictionarymatch will run alongsid the regex engin 2026 08 12 13 30 diana bob what happen if there s a comma in the term standard csv escap 2026 08 12 13 32 bob yeah i m use the python csv modul with quot _ minim i ll add a test case for quot term\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edc9244e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"id\": \"d9aa72bd1d956a20\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3256900625100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.60781103, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edc9244e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1112, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:07\", \"token_count\": 335, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-25\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Redaction Preview Highlighting\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 08:40] Charlie**: Implementing the highlighting logic for the preview overlay. Pulling the region coordinates straight from the YAML redaction-policy config so it stays in sync with whatever regions are defined there.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 08:42] Charlie**: Highlighting engine is in — it maps each YAML-configured region to a bounding box on the overlay shell.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 08:43] Diana**: Checking it now. Looking solid so far.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 08:44] Diana**: One issue: highlights are slightly offset on rotated pages.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 08:46] Charlie**: Fixed — wasn't accounting for the `page.rotate` property in the coordinate transform.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 12:58] Diana**: Verified rotated pages are highlighting correctly now. Overlay and highlighting together meet the visual review requirement.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 14:00] Diana**: Preview overlay is accepted — we're good to close this.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 14:26] Alice**: Good, this gives reviewers real confidence the system's doing the right thing.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 25 slack thread redact preview highlight channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 06 last activ 2026 08 08 2026 08 06 08 40 charli implement the highlight logic for the preview overlay pull the region coordin straight from the yaml redact polici config so it stay in sync with whatev region are defin there 2026 08 06 08 42 charli highlight engin is in it map each yaml configur region to a bound box on the overlay shell 2026 08 06 08 43 diana check it now look solid so far 2026 08 06 08 44 diana one issu highlight are slight offset on rotat page 2026 08 06 08 46 charli fix wasn t account for the page rotat properti in the coordin transform 2026 08 08 12 58 diana verifi rotat page are highlight correct now overlay and highlight togeth meet the visual review requir 2026 08 08 14 00 diana preview overlay is accept we re good to close this 2026 08 08 14 26 alic good this give review real confid the system s do the right thing\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee223e6c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-redaction-preview-highlighting.md\", \"id\": \"9441a46edb882406\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3228563135100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.5983652, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-redaction-preview-highlighting.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee223e6c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-redaction-preview-highlighting.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-redaction-preview-highlighting.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1174, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:47\", \"token_count\": 333, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-37\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Title**: Validate batch runs under a network-denied harness\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild a reproducible offline test harness that denies network access, then execute a full batch run under it to validate the strict air-gapped claim, depending on the completed AES-256 encryption pipeline. The offline batch run completed and was signed o