render librari with no local fix yet\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee65b87c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-46-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes.md\", \"id\": \"315ff6b01a17e19a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3925351768083519, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2833422382976456, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6473187, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-46-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee65b87c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-46-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-46-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 974, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:45\", \"token_count\": 505, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Test Logs\\n\\nReproduction notes for the high-DPI coordinate misalignment reported for CIPH-46, first reproduced 2026-08-17.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Repro steps\\n\\n1. Open a PDF on a display reporting a scale factor above 1.0 (tested at 150% and 200%).\\n\\n2. Compare the redaction preview overlay's reported box coordinates against the coordinates the rendering library reports for the same region.\\n\\n3. At scale factors above 1.0, the overlay box is offset from the actual text region, with the offset growing as scale factor increases.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nThe misalignment reproduces consistently at both tested scale factors. It does not reproduce at 100% scale.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nRoot cause has not been isolated as part of this reproduction pass; this note only establishes that the defect reproduces and under which display conditions.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 test log reproduct note for the high dpi coordin misalign report for ciph 46 first reproduc 2026 08 17 sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 repro step 1 open a pdf on a display report a scale factor abov 10 test at 150 and 200 2 compar the redact preview overlay s report box coordin against the coordin the render librari report for the same region 3 at scale factor abov 10 the overlay box is offset from the actual text region with the offset grow a scale factor increas sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 result the misalign reproduc consist at both test scale factor it doe not reproduc at 100 scale sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 status root caus ha not been isol a part of this reproduct pas this note onli establish that the defect reproduc and under which display condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee87b8968a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"id\": \"99b368dd772283f8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3777957868083519, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2833422382976456, \"vector_similarity\": 0.5981874, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee87b8968a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 987, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:14\", \"token_count\": 453, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-64\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Telemetry Opt-Out Verification\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-24\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:31] Diana**: Finished the network trace tests. With the flag set to `false`, there is zero outbound traffic to the telemetry endpoints.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:45] Bob**: Excellent. PR #91 is merged and verified.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:46] Alice**: Thanks Diana. This is a big one for our compliance audit.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:49] Evan**: I've updated the Docker image to include the environment variable support.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:56] Diana**: I also tested the GUI toggle. It correctly updates the config file and requires a restart to take effect, which is exactly what we wanted.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:57] Alice**: Closing. Great work everyone. :lock:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 64 slack thread telemetri opt out verif channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 24 2026 08 24 13 31 diana finish the network trace test with the flag set to fals there is zero outbound traffic to the telemetri endpoint 2026 08 24 13 45 bob excel pr 91 is merg and verifi 2026 08 24 13 46 alic thank diana this is a big one for our complianc audit 2026 08 24 13 49 evan i ve updat the docker imag to includ the environ variabl support 2026 08 24 13 56 diana i also test the gui toggl it correct updat the config file and requir a restart to take effect which is exact what we want 2026 08 24 13 57 alic close great work everyon lock\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee11c7b28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-telemetry-opt-out-verify.md\", \"id\": \"5d27e50f6a0dd358\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3372231635100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6462547, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-telemetry-opt-out-verify.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee11c7b28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-telemetry-opt-out-verify.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-telemetry-opt-out-verify.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 783, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:01\", \"token_count\": 249, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-32\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:05] Diana**: Building the offline harness for the air-gapped mode claim — network access denied at the OS level so we get a reproducible offline run instead of just trusting the binary not to phone home.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:06] Alice**: Make sure to check startup specifically — if any check blocks waiting on the network before it gives up, that's a problem even if everything after it runs fine offline.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:32] Diana**: That's on the list. I want to see it fail closed fast, not hang.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:43] Bob**: How does this interact with the offline auth work? If the license check can't reach anything, does it fail open or just error out?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:46] Diana**: I'll run that combination through the harness too once the base setup is solid — good thing to catch here rather than in the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 12:16] Evan**: Let me know when it's ready. I want to run the benchmark scripts through it too, once we have real offline numbers to compare against online.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 32 slack thread offlin test har channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 06 2026 08 06 09 05 diana build the offlin har for the air gap mode claim network access deni at the o level so we get a reproduc offlin run instead of just trust the binari not to phone home 2026 08 06 09 06 alic make sure to check startup specif if ani check block wait on the network befor it give up that s a problem even if everyth after it run fine offlin 2026 08 06 09 32 diana that s on the list i want to see it fail close fast not hang 2026 08 06 09 43 bob how doe this interact with the offlin auth work if the licens check can t reach anyth doe it fail open or just error out 2026 08 06 09 46 diana i ll run that combin through the har too onc the base setup is solid good thing to catch here rather than in the field 2026 08 06 12 16 evan let me know when it s readi i want to run the benchmark script through it too onc we have real offlin number to compar against onlin\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edc1ce248a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-offline-harness.md\", \"id\": \"3f083453d3871409\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33505279551005684, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63902014, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-offline-harness.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edc1ce248a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-offline-harness.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-offline-harness.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1135, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:13\", \"token_count\": 322, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-63\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:12] Bob**: The `telemetry_enabled` flag is now fully integrated into the CLI and the API. Default is set to `true` but it's easily overridden in `config.yaml`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:37] Evan**: Can we also support an environment variable like `DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1`? That would be easier for the Docker deployments.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:43] Bob**: Good call. I'll add that to the `Settings` loader.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:46] Diana**: I noticed that even when it's off, the app still tries to ping the update server on startup. Does that count as telemetry?\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:57] Alice**: Update checks are fine, that's a security requirement. But we shouldn't send any machine IDs with that request.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:13] Bob**: It's a clean GET request, no headers other than the current version string.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:16] Diana**: Okay, I'll verify that with a packet capture tomorrow.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 63 slack thread telemetri opt out flag channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 22 2026 08 22 14 12 bob the telemetri _ enabl flag is now fulli integr into the cli and the api default is set to true but it s easili overridden in config yaml 2026 08 22 14 37 evan can we also support an environ variabl like disabl _ telemetri 1 that would be easier for the docker deploy 2026 08 22 14 43 bob good call i ll add that to the set loader 2026 08 22 14 46 diana i notic that even when it s off the app still tri to ping the updat server on startup doe that count a telemetri 2026 08 22 14 57 alic updat check are fine that s a secur requir but we shouldn t send ani machin id with that request 2026 08 22 15 13 bob it s a clean get request no header other than the current version string 2026 08 22 15 16 diana okay i ll verifi that with a packet captur tomorrow\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edcb1d808a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"id\": \"48914573979d0262\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3341125235100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6358859, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edcb1d808a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1015, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:07\", \"token_count\": 320, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Why a Harness, Not a One-Off VM\\n\\nAn earlier air-gapped check (see the manual single-VM USB-transfer test) proved the CLI *can* run offline, but it wasn't repeatable — every run required hand-configuring a disconnected machine. T027 calls for a harness that reliably and automatically denies network access on every run, so the offline claim can be re-verified continuously rather than checked once by hand.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Harness Design\\n\\n- Runs the batch CLI inside a dedicated Linux network namespace (`ip netns`) with no interfaces attached except loopback, rather than relying on a physically air-gapped machine.\\n\\n- A wrapper script asserts the namespace has zero routable interfaces before invoking the CLI, and fails the harness run outright — rather than silently proceeding — if any route to the outside world is detected.\\n\\n- Harness output is a pass/fail plus a captured syscall-level network-attempt log, so any code path that *tries* to reach the network, even if it degrades gracefully, is visible for follow-up.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nDenies network access reliably and repeatably across local test runs. The harness is not yet wired into CI (it currently runs manually), and it validates network denial only — it does not itself certify the full offline batch run for compliance purposes; that sign-off is a separate step.\\n\\n*Status*: Active. Harness reliably enforces network denial; CI integration and any compliance certification are separate, not-yet-complete steps.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 whi a har not a one off vm an earlier air gap check see the manual singl vm usb transfer test prove the cli can run offlin but it wasn t repeat everi run requir hand configur a disconnect machin t027 call for a har that reliabl and automat deni network access on everi run so the offlin claim can be re verifi continu rather than check onc by hand sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 har design run the batch cli insid a dedic linux network namespac ip netn with no interfac attach except loopback rather than reli on a physic air gap machin a wrapper script assert the namespac ha zero routabl interfac befor invok the cli and fail the har run outright rather than silent proceed if ani rout to the outsid world is detect har output is a pas fail plus a captur syscal level network attempt log so ani code path that tri to reach the network even if it degrad grace is visibl for follow up sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 status deni network access reliabl and repeat across local test run the har is not yet wire into ci it current run manual and it valid network denial onli it doe not itself certifi the full offlin batch run for complianc purpos that sign off is a separ step status activ har reliabl enforc network denial ci integr and ani complianc certif are separ not yet complet step\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eec625ae8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"id\": \"d8a36cad3ad1e56e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33380829351005686, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6348718, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eec625ae8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1618, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:20\", \"token_count\": 465, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-54\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Electron IPC Bridge\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 11:11] Bob**: Just finished the IPC bridge between the Electron main process and the React frontend. We can now pass configuration objects directly through to the batch CLI tool it wraps.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 11:43] Evan**: I'm seeing some issues with the process state when a large batch is running. The GUI freezes up because the IPC channel is getting flooded with progress updates.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 12:04] Bob**: We should probably throttle those updates. We don't need a message for every single file if it's a 10,000 document batch.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 12:07] Charlie**: Or use a separate worker thread for the CLI monitoring?\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 12:19] Evan**: I'll try debouncing the updates in the main process first. If that doesn't work, I'll move the child process management to a background utility.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 13:46] Alice**: @Evan, @Bob, let's keep it simple for now. Even a 1-second update interval is fine for the UI.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 13:51] Diana**: Agree. As long as it doesn't look like it's crashed, users are happy.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 54 slack thread electron ipc bridg channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 16 2026 08 16 1111 bob just finish the ipc bridg between the electron main process and the react frontend we can now pas configur object direct through to the batch cli tool it wrap 2026 08 16 11 43 evan i m see some issu with the process state when a larg batch is run the gui freez up becaus the ipc channel is get flood with progress updat 2026 08 16 12 04 bob we should probabl throttl those updat we don t need a messag for everi singl file if it s a 10 000 document batch 2026 08 16 12 07 charli or use a separ worker thread for the cli monitor 2026 08 16 12 19 evan i ll tri debounc the updat in the main process first if that doesn t work i ll move the child process manag to a background util 2026 08 16 13 46 alic evan bob let s keep it simpl for now even a1 second updat interv is fine for the ui 2026 08 16 13 51 diana agre a long a it doesn t look like it s crash user are happi\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee151ce68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-electron-ipc-bridge.md\", \"id\": \"7a1cfdb37ed5d8de\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3318109835100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6282141, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-electron-ipc-bridge.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee151ce68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-electron-ipc-bridge.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-electron-ipc-bridge.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1152, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:59\", \"token_count\": 343, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-47\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Redaction Profile Export Verification\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 14:35] Diana**: Final verification on the redaction-profile export is looking solid — I checked the exported payloads against the REST API contract, and the fields line up with what Bob shipped for the existing endpoints.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 16:18] Alice**: Awesome. @Diana did you test it with the large profiles we generated for the stress test? Any latency issues?\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 16:26] Diana**: Latency is negligible since it's just a JSON dump. The largest one (about 4MB) came back in under 150ms.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:42] Bob**: I also added a `Content-Disposition` header to the response, so if you hit it from a browser, it'll prompt to save as `profile_export_[timestamp].json`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:43] Charlie**: @Bob helps a lot with the CLI parity work I'm doing. I can basically pipe this straight into the local engine for debugging.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:46] Alice**: Great work everyone. Calling this done — export matches the REST contract.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:49] Bob**: :raised_hands:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 47 slack thread redact profil export verif channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 16 2026 08 16 14 35 diana final verif on the redact profil export is look solid i check the export payload against the rest api contract and the field line up with what bob ship for the exist endpoint 2026 08 16 16 18 alic awesom diana did you test it with the larg profil we generat for the stress test ani latenc issu 2026 08 16 16 26 diana latenc is neglig sinc it s just a json dump the largest one about 4mb came back in under 150ms 2026 08 16 17 42 bob i also ad a content disposit header to the respons so if you hit it from a browser it ll prompt to save a profil _ export _ timestamp json 2026 08 16 17 43 charli bob help a lot with the cli pariti work i m do i can basic pipe this straight into the local engin for debug 2026 08 16 17 46 alic great work everyon call this done export match the rest contract 2026 08 16 17 49 bob rais _ hand\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edbde0848a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"id\": \"5ed77310c4e63c72\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33111645351005686, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.625899, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edbde0848a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1141, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:17\", \"token_count\": 338, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-23\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Storage Quota Halt Verification and Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:19] Diana**: Verification done on the disk monitor. Filled the disk with dummy data and confirmed the engine halts writes once it hits the configured 500MB floor. That meets the requirement — calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:46] Evan**: Good. I'll keep an eye on it as we add more features, don't want the threshold logic drifting.\\n\\n**[2026-09-15 10:06] Evan**: Reopening this. Production-like batches are tripping the 500MB hard halt before they've done any useful work — it's too aggressive for how these jobs actually run.\\n\\n**[2026-09-15 10:07] Diana**: Makes sense, a flat cutoff doesn't account for how much a batch has already written before it gets close to the line.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:30] Bob**: Refactored the monitor to use a 10% buffer tolerance above the quota instead of the hard 500MB halt. Root cause was that hard cutoff having no soft buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:31] Diana**: Nice.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:39] Evan**: That should behave a lot better under real batch sizes. I'll re-test against the same production-like batches that tripped it before.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:58] Evan**: Re-tested — no premature halts on the batches that failed before. Looks good.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 23 slack thread storag quota halt verif and reopen channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 06 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 08 06 09 19 diana verif done on the disk monitor fill the disk with dummi data and confirm the engin halt write onc it hit the configur 500mb floor that meet the requir call this done 2026 08 06 09 46 evan good i ll keep an eye on it a we add more featur don t want the threshold logic drift 2026 09 15 10 06 evan reopen this product like batch are trip the 500mb hard halt befor they ve done ani use work it s too aggress for how these job actual run 2026 09 15 10 07 diana make sens a flat cutoff doesn t account for how much a batch ha alreadi written befor it get close to the line 2026 09 18 09 30 bob refactor the monitor to use a 10 buffer toler abov the quota instead of the hard 500mb halt root caus wa that hard cutoff have no soft buffer 2026 09 18 09 31 diana nice 2026 09 18 09 39 evan that should behav a lot better under real batch size i ll re test against the same product like batch that trip it befor 2026 09 18 09 58 evan re test no prematur halt on the batch that fail befor look good\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee05f4148a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"id\": \"c56dc1694b3ef534\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33079878351005687, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6248401, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee05f4148a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1374, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:12\", \"token_count\": 403, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-39\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License Audit\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-09\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 11:13] Diana**: Starting the third-party license audit across the dependency tree — need a full inventory before we sign off on anything for release.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 12:37] Alice**: Watch closely for GPL or AGPL. Our client agreements rule out shipping copyleft code in the core engine.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 12:46] Diana**: That's exactly what I'm scanning for, using license-checker against the dependency manifests to flag anything outside MIT/Apache/BSD.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:19] Bob**: Are you following transitive dependencies too? A clean top-level library can still pull in something restrictive underneath.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:24] Diana**: Yes, doing a recursive pass, not just the direct dependencies.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:51] Evan**: Want a hand with the Docker base image layers once the app-level scan is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 14:07] Diana**: That'd help. Still working through the results — nothing conclusive to report yet, I'll have the full inventory soon.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 39 slack thread licens audit channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 09 2026 08 09 11 13 diana start the third parti licens audit across the depend tree need a full inventori befor we sign off on anyth for releas 2026 08 09 12 37 alic watch close for gpl or agpl our client agreement rule out ship copyleft code in the core engin 2026 08 09 12 46 diana that s exact what i m scan for use licens checker against the depend manifest to flag anyth outsid mit apach bsd 2026 08 09 13 19 bob are you follow transit depend too a clean top level librari can still pull in someth restrict underneath 2026 08 09 13 24 diana yes do a recurs pas not just the direct depend 2026 08 09 13 51 evan want a hand with the docker base imag layer onc the app level scan is done 2026 08 09 14 07 diana that d help still work through the result noth conclus to report yet i ll have the full inventori soon\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0111388a991