ori 2026 08 18 alic task creat open open the task becaus an async batch api schedul is need for higher throughput 2026 08 25 diana i o race block block block after find a concurr i o race that cut throughput by rough 10 depend on the multi thread work\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee7e45908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"id\": \"6b3cd42efe279a7b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3938936668083519, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2833422382976456, \"vector_similarity\": 0.651847, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee7e45908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1019, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:21\", \"token_count\": 519, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## What was added\\n\\nAn asynchronous scheduler that accepts batch API jobs and dispatches them to worker threads without blocking the request path, building on the multi-threading work already integrated into the batch CLI.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## Design\\n\\nJobs are queued with a job ID returned immediately to the caller; a separate status endpoint reports progress. Workers pull from the same queue used by the multi-threaded batch path.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis note covers the scheduler's implementation and design only. It does not cover any concurrency issues found during later evaluation of the scheduler under load; those are separate from what this note documents.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load what wa ad an asynchron schedul that accept batch api job and dispatch them to worker thread without block the request path build on the multi thread work alreadi integr into the batch cli sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load design job are queu with a job id return immedi to the caller a separ status endpoint report progress worker pull from the same queue use by the multi thread batch path sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load scope this note cover the schedul s implement and design onli it doe not cover ani concurr issu found dure later evalu of the schedul under load those are separ from what this note document\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eed7bad08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"id\": \"e00a9a695a57f07d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3805027168083519, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2833422382976456, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6072105, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eed7bad08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 956, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:06\", \"token_count\": 412, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## What Was Run\\n\\nA full batch redaction run was executed under the offline test harness (T027) with network access denied, using a local sample document set. The run depended on the completed AES-256 at-rest encryption pipeline (T021), since offline output still needs to be encrypted without any network-based key service.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nThe batch completed successfully end-to-end with the network denied: no network-dependent call blocked the run, and local policy parsing worked entirely from bundled definitions.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Noted Issue: 45-Second Licence-Check Hang\\n\\nThe run was not clean — the HTTP client attempted to verify the license key against a remote server before timing out and falling back to the cached local license, adding roughly 45 seconds of startup delay. This is logged as a known issue, not something this sign-off waives.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Scope of This Sign-off\\n\\nThis sign-off is **preliminary** and covers functional completion of a batch run offline only. It is explicitly **not** a compliance certification — it does not cover side-channel analysis, physical security, or any regulatory attestation. No patient records or clinical data were used in this test run.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 what wa run a full batch redact run wa execut under the offlin test har t027 with network access deni use a local sampl document set the run depend on the complet ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin t021 sinc offlin output still need to be encrypt without ani network base key servic sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 result the batch complet success end to end with the network deni no network depend call block the run and local polici pars work entir from bundl definit sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 note issu 45 second licenc check hang the run wa not clean the http client attempt to verifi the licens key against a remot server befor time out and fall back to the cach local licens ad rough 45 second of startup delay this is log a a known issu not someth this sign off waif sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 scope of this sign off this sign off is preliminari and cover function complet of a batch run offlin onli it is explicit not a complianc certif it doe not cover side channel analysi physic secur or ani regulatori attest no patient record or clinic data were use in this test run\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee9b9e6a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"id\": \"3766c87791acc1a0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33304752351005684, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6323359, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee9b9e6a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1322, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:55\", \"token_count\": 456, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-47\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Redaction Profile Export Verification\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 14:35] Diana**: Final verification on the redaction-profile export is looking solid — I checked the exported payloads against the REST API contract, and the fields line up with what Bob shipped for the existing endpoints.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 16:18] Alice**: Awesome. @Diana did you test it with the large profiles we generated for the stress test? Any latency issues?\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 16:26] Diana**: Latency is negligible since it's just a JSON dump. The largest one (about 4MB) came back in under 150ms.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:42] Bob**: I also added a `Content-Disposition` header to the response, so if you hit it from a browser, it'll prompt to save as `profile_export_[timestamp].json`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:43] Charlie**: @Bob helps a lot with the CLI parity work I'm doing. I can basically pipe this straight into the local engine for debugging.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:46] Alice**: Great work everyone. Calling this done — export matches the REST contract.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 17:49] Bob**: :raised_hands:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 47 slack thread redact profil export verif channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 16 2026 08 16 14 35 diana final verif on the redact profil export is look solid i check the export payload against the rest api contract and the field line up with what bob ship for the exist endpoint 2026 08 16 16 18 alic awesom diana did you test it with the larg profil we generat for the stress test ani latenc issu 2026 08 16 16 26 diana latenc is neglig sinc it s just a json dump the largest one about 4mb came back in under 150ms 2026 08 16 17 42 bob i also ad a content disposit header to the respons so if you hit it from a browser it ll prompt to save a profil _ export _ timestamp json 2026 08 16 17 43 charli bob help a lot with the cli pariti work i m do i can basic pipe this straight into the local engin for debug 2026 08 16 17 46 alic great work everyon call this done export match the rest contract 2026 08 16 17 49 bob rais _ hand\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edbde0848a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"id\": \"5ed77310c4e63c72\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3301226285100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.62258625, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edbde0848a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-redaction-profile-verify.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1141, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:17\", \"token_count\": 338, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-26\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Prototype\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:30] Bob**: Starting on the replication handshake for the zero-trust node sync. First requirement is that two nodes have to authenticate each other before either one accepts replicated entries.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:37] Evan**: How's a node proving who it is right now?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:38] Bob**: Each node has a registered identity it presents at connect time. If the peer doesn't recognize it, the connection gets dropped before any data moves.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:49] Charlie**: Does the handshake add noticeable overhead to the redaction jobs running on the same box?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:40] Bob**: Negligible so far — it's a short exchange before the sync session opens, nothing that touches the active redaction path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:41] Diana**: What's next after the prototype?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 11:47] Bob**: Need to check it holds up under real network delay, not just on my two test nodes on the same switch. That's the next pass.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 26 slack thread node sync handshak prototyp channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 06 2026 08 06 09 30 bob start on the replic handshak for the zero trust node sync first requir is that two node have to authent each other befor either one accept replic entri 2026 08 06 09 37 evan how s a node prove who it is right now 2026 08 06 09 38 bob each node ha a regist ident it present at connect time if the peer doesn t recogn it the connect get drop befor ani data move 2026 08 06 09 49 charli doe the handshak add notic overhead to the redact job run on the same box 2026 08 06 10 40 bob neglig so far it s a short exchang befor the sync session open noth that touch the activ redact path 2026 08 06 10 41 diana what s next after the prototyp 2026 08 06 11 47 bob need to check it hold up under real network delay not just on my two test node on the same switch that s the next pas\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ede2c2fa8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"id\": \"4bd5b5740e6d4a32\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32976999351005687, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6214108, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ede2c2fa8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1079, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:46\", \"token_count\": 317, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-03\\n\\n# Slack Thread: REST API Scaffolding and TempFile Policy\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:09] Bob**: Starting on the REST API scaffolding. Going with FastAPI for the layer. It's lightweight and the auto-generated OpenAPI docs will save us a ton of time.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:39] Diana**: +1 for FastAPI. Can we ensure we have request validation schemas for the upload endpoint? We don't want malformed JSON crashing the engine.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:43] Bob**: Already on it. Using Pydantic for the `RedactionRequest` model. Scaffold is up and running in the `api-scaffold` branch.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 10:50] Bob**: Quick update on the file handling. I'm implementing a strict temp-file cleanup policy.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 10:56] Diana**: How are we handling cleanup? If a request fails mid-stream, do we leave orphaned files on the container?\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:15] Bob**: No, I'm using a `try...finally` block with a context manager. Files are wiped immediately after the redaction job completes or errors out. No PII should ever persist in `/tmp`.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:16] Diana**: What about memory-mapped files for larger uploads?\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:33] Bob**: For now, everything is streamed. We might need `mmap` later, but for the MVP, the context manager approach is safer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:47] Diana**: I'll start the security audit once you merge the policy. We need to be 100% sure about that cleanup logic.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 03 slack thread rest api scaffold and tempfil polici channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 14 2026 06 14 09 09 bob start on the rest api scaffold go with fastapi for the layer it s lightweight and the auto generat openapi doc will save u a ton of time 2026 06 14 09 39 diana 1 for fastapi can we ensur we have request valid schema for the upload endpoint we don t want malform json crash the engin 2026 06 14 09 43 bob alreadi on it use pydant for the redactionrequest model scaffold is up and run in the api scaffold branch 2026 06 14 10 50 bob quick updat on the file handl i m implement a strict temp file cleanup polici 2026 06 14 10 56 diana how are we handl cleanup if a request fail mid stream do we leav orphan file on the contain 2026 06 14 11 15 bob no i m use a tri final block with a context manag file are wipe immedi after the redact job complet or error out no pii should ever persist in tmp 2026 06 14 11 16 diana what about memori map file for larger upload 2026 06 14 11 33 bob for now everyth is stream we might need mmap later but for the mvp the context manag approach is safer 2026 06 14 11 47 diana i ll start the secur audit onc you merg the polici we need to be 100 sure about that cleanup logic\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edecdf068a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"id\": \"0cf7ef3515c36d5b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3294777545100569, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20478107644293841, \"vector_similarity\": 0.62043667, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edecdf068a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:36\", \"token_count\": 436, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-51\\n\\n# Slack Thread: CSV Dictionary Rule Test Notes\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 13:21] Diana**: Ran the rule test against the merged CSV dictionary — it's passing clean, including the terms layered on top of the HIPAA patterns.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 13:47] Bob**: Good, and that's sitting on top of the financial-detection baseline. No regressions there?\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 14:13] Diana**: Confirmed — reran the financial-detection suite too, still green. Calling the CSV matcher rule test complete.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 14:16] Alice**: Nice, thanks Diana. That closes out the dictionary matching piece.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 51 slack thread csv dictionari rule test note channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 16 2026 08 16 13 21 diana ran the rule test against the merg csv dictionari it s pass clean includ the term layer on top of the hipaa pattern 2026 08 16 13 47 bob good and that s sit on top of the financi detect baselin no regress there 2026 08 16 14 13 diana confirm reran the financi detect suit too still green call the csv matcher rule test complet 2026 08 16 14 16 alic nice thank diana that close out the dictionari match piec\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db23